    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0441" n="323" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">702.9493/55: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase—Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-01-14T11:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 14,
                                1928—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 14—11:05
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>28.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>7. It is my continued hope that events may shape themselves in such a way that I
                    may find it expedient in the near future (sometime in February would be
                    suitable) to go to Shanghai, at which time every effort will be made by me to
                    effect a satisfactory settlement of the Nanking outrages. …</p>
                <p>8. Copy sent to Tokio by mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
